## 1. Product scope and positioning

Define this clearly before any code:

- **Audience:** India‑first (multi‑language later), plus a “World” section; think of default feed as “India Now,” with a tab for “World Now.”  
- **Content types (verticals):** AI, tech & science, politics, business, sports, entertainment, art & culture, “top trending” (cross‑category). These map directly to categories you’ll get from most news APIs. [worldnewsapi](https://worldnewsapi.com/docs/news-sources/india-news-api/)
- **Differentiator:**  
  - Ultra‑light frontend that works on 2G/weak 4G.  
  - Source‑first (show logo + link for every article, multiple sources per story).  
  - Clear labels like “Raw wire,” “Opinion,” “AI‑summary,” and “Source list” to avoid hidden bias.  

Decide early if you’ll **only aggregate + lightly summarize** (simpler compliance) or also allow **original articles/op‑eds**; I’d recommend phase 1 = aggregation only.

