## 2. High‑level system architecture

Think of four main layers (you can start monolithic and move to services later): [akhmadreiza.medium](https://akhmadreiza.medium.com/news-aggregator-system-design-8a036f0f048b)

1. **Ingestion layer (pulling news):**  
   - Connectors to external **News APIs** (NewsAPI, NewsData.io, mediastack, World News API, etc.). [mediastack](https://mediastack.com/sources/india-news-api)
   - RSS/Atom feed collectors for Indian outlets that have feeds. [akhmadreiza.medium](https://akhmadreiza.medium.com/news-aggregator-system-design-8a036f0f048b)
   - Optional: controlled web scrapers (e.g., for government websites, press releases) where allowed.  

2. **Processing layer:**  
   - **Normalization:** convert all sources into one internal schema: `Article { id, title, summary, fullText?, url, source, language, country, category[], publishedAt, rawTags }`. [akhmadreiza.medium](https://akhmadreiza.medium.com/news-aggregator-system-design-8a036f0f048b)
   - **Deduplication:** cluster same story across sources by URL similarity + title similarity + publication time; keep a canonical “story id” with multiple links attached. [blog.stackademic](https://blog.stackademic.com/designing-a-scalable-news-aggregator-system-google-news-scale-a-deep-dive-with-full-explanation-fc39ee5ea13b)
   - **Categorization & tagging:**  
     - Start with API categories (business, sports, tech, etc.). [newsapi](https://newsapi.org)
     - Add your AI models later for finer tags like “AI policy,” “EVs,” “startup funding.”  
   - **Ranking:** sort primarily by time + source reliability; later add signals like user interest, clickthrough, and “not seen before.” [systemdesignhandbook](https://www.systemdesignhandbook.com/guides/google-news-system-design/)

3. **Storage & query layer:**  
   - **Primary DB:** PostgreSQL (articles, sources, users, preferences).  
   - **Search/index:** OpenSearch/Elasticsearch or even Postgres full‑text search initially for title/summary search and fast category queries. [blog.stackademic](https://blog.stackademic.com/designing-a-scalable-news-aggregator-system-google-news-scale-a-deep-dive-with-full-explanation-fc39ee5ea13b)
   - **Cache:** Redis for top feeds (e.g., “India Top,” “AI Today”) to serve in milliseconds.  

4. **Delivery layer (API + web app):**  
   - Backend HTTP API (REST or GraphQL) for feeds, search, user profiles.  
   - Frontend: server‑rendered web app + PWA (installable on Android, works offline) with a **text‑first, minimal‑JS UI** to support low bandwidth. [birdhousewebsites](https://birdhousewebsites.com/blog/designing-for-low-bandwidth-users-essential-tips-and/)

This structure lets you keep ingestion and heavy processing on the server while shipping almost pure HTML + a bit of JS to the client.

