## 3. Data sources and authenticity

To stay “raw and crystal clear” while covering India + world almost real‑time, mix several APIs + some RSS:  

- **India‑focused APIs:**  
  - World News API (filter `source-country=in`, categories like politics, business, tech, sports, etc.). [worldnewsapi](https://worldnewsapi.com/docs/news-sources/india-news-api/)
  - mediastack (use `country=in` and specific categories). [mediastack](https://mediastack.com/sources/india-news-api)
  - NewsAPI top headlines from India (`country=in`). [newsapi](https://newsapi.org/s/india-news-api)

- **Worldwide coverage:**  
  - NewsAPI for global headlines and 150,000+ sources (14 languages, 55 countries). [newsapi](https://newsapi.org)
  - NewsData.io (80,000+ sources, 206 countries, 6 years of historical data) — can be your backbone for global + historical queries. [newsdata](https://newsdata.io)

Guidelines for authenticity and no‑bias:  

- Always store and display: **source name, favicon/logo, original headline, timestamp, direct link**, and country/language. [newsdata](https://newsdata.io)
- For each “story cluster,” show **multiple sources** (e.g., Indian national paper, regional outlet, international wire) so users see varied framing.  
- Keep AI involvement transparent: if you generate summaries, mark them explicitly as “AI‑generated summary based on these sources.”  

