## 5. Recommended tech stack (pragmatic but “top‑notch”)

Given your full‑stack + AI background and preference for production‑ready code:  

- **Backend / API / ingestion:**  
  - Language: **TypeScript** (Node.js) or **Go**; TS will integrate very nicely with Copilot.  
  - Framework: **NestJS** (Node) or a clean modular Express/Koa setup; Nest gives you DI, modules, and structured code from day 1.  
  - Background jobs for ingestion:  
    - Use something like **BullMQ** (Redis‑based) or simple cron jobs initially to call APIs every X minutes per category/region.  

- **Database & search:**  
  - **PostgreSQL** with Prisma/TypeORM for typed models.  
  - Start with Postgres full‑text search; move to OpenSearch/Elasticsearch once you need richer search and analytics. [blog.stackademic](https://blog.stackademic.com/designing-a-scalable-news-aggregator-system-google-news-scale-a-deep-dive-with-full-explanation-fc39ee5ea13b)

- **Frontend:**  
  - **Next.js (App Router) or Remix**: server‑side rendering + file‑based routing + good caching.  
  - Strict TypeScript, no heavy UI kit; build your own minimal, responsive components in plain CSS (or a very light utility layer).  
  - Make it a **PWA** (manifest + service worker) so users can “install” it and get offline caching.  

- **Infrastructure:**  
  - Start on a simple VPS or managed platform (Render/Fly.io/Vercel + managed Postgres).  
  - Put a CDN (Cloudflare, etc.) in front for caching, SSL, and edge performance.  

- **AI utilities (later phases):**  
  - Separate “AI worker” service that:  
    - Summarises long articles into 2–3 bullet points.  
    - Classifies into more granular tags.  
    - Detects near‑duplicates beyond simple textual similarity (e.g., using embeddings).  

