## 6. Development roadmap you can follow with Copilot

Think in phases; each phase shippable, with production hygiene from day 1.

### Phase 1 – Core aggregator MVP (4–6 weeks)

Goal: Read‑only, blazing‑fast public site with India + world feeds.

- **Week 1: Domain model + ingestion MVP**  
  - Define TypeScript interfaces for `Article`, `Source`, `Category`, `Region`, `UserPreference`.  
  - Implement ingestion from **one India API** and **one global API** (e.g., World News API + NewsAPI/NewsData.io) with simple cron/task runner. [worldnewsapi](https://worldnewsapi.com/docs/news-sources/india-news-api/)
  - Normalize into Postgres, log ingestion metrics per run.  

- **Week 2: Processing basics**  
  - Add deduplication (hashing normalized titles + URLs; cluster by time window).  
  - Basic category mapping (API categories → your unified categories).  

- **Week 3: API + first frontend**  
  - Build REST endpoints: `/feed?region=in&category=ai`, `/feed/top`, `/search?q=...`, `/story/:id`.  
  - Next.js SSR frontend:  
    - Home = “India Top Now”; tabs for “World,” “AI,” “Politics,” etc.  
    - Each article card: title, source, published time, short summary (from API if provided), “Read at [source]” link.  

- **Week 4: Performance + low‑bandwidth polish**  
  - Implement text‑only mode, lazy‑load thumbnails, aggressive HTML/CSS/JS minification. [birdhousewebsites](https://birdhousewebsites.com/blog/designing-for-low-bandwidth-users-essential-tips-and/)
  - Add simple PWA manifest and basic service worker caching last N feeds.  

### Phase 2 – Personalization, AI assist, and transparency (4–8 weeks)

- **User accounts and preferences:**  
  - Allow login (email/OTP or OAuth), favorite categories (AI, politics, sports), preferred languages, and “bias controls” (e.g., slider for “more diverse sources”).  
- **Transparency UI:**  
  - On story page: show list of all sources in that cluster with labels “Indian national,” “Regional,” “International,” “Wire,” etc.  
- **AI summarization & tagging:**  
  - Background worker to generate 2–3 bullet summaries per story; mark clearly as AI summary.  
  - Add richer tags (e.g., “semiconductors,” “EV policy,” “budget 2027”).  

### Phase 3 – Original content + community (optional)

- Add **editorial CMS** where you/your team can publish original explainers, analysis pieces, and long‑form articles.  
- Carefully label these as “Opinion” or “Explainer” vs aggregated “Raw News.”  

Throughout all phases, enforce: code reviews (even if it’s you + AI), tests for critical flows, logging and monitoring.

